# Quitting saves what the reviewer did first: three hunks approved and q, typed faster than the
# marks save, are all there when the review opens again, at the hunk where the reviewer quit.
# A terminal tells a held key by time alone, so `k j` between taps of Space keeps each one a
# press of its own there.
# Both front ends end their smoke runs with it, since it relaunches.
launch --demo
file src/compat.rs
key 0
state
expect "progress":\{"files":\[6,54\],"hunks":\[15,292\],"auto_approved":6\}
rapid key space k j space k j space q
exited
launch --demo-revision 1
expect "progress":\{"files":\[7,54\],"hunks":\[18,292\],"auto_approved":6\}
# The review opens where the reviewer quit.
state
expect "selected":"src/compat.rs"
expect "hunk":2,"hunks"

# While quitting waits it takes no new marks, and quitting again drops nothing: of two approvals
# before q and a third after it, then q again, both approvals before q are recorded, which
# finishes the file.
file src/generated/schema.rs
key 0
state
expect "progress":\{"files":\[7,54\],"hunks":\[18,292\],"auto_approved":6\}
rapid key space k j space q space q
exited
launch --demo-revision 1
expect "progress":\{"files":\[8,54\],"hunks":\[20,292\],"auto_approved":6\}
